          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em derived smooth manifold
            is the generalization of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+differential+geometry"} derived differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            for
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+algebra"} smooth algebra
            = succeed "-rings):" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
          %p
            it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} structured (∞,1)-topos
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            of functions is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebra"} smooth (∞,1)-algebra
          %h2#motivation_correction_of_limits Motivation: correction of limits
          %p
            According to the general logic of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %em derived smooth manifold
            serves to
            %em correct
            certain
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            but do not have the correct
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomological behaviour
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transversal+map"} transversal map
          %h3#pontrjaginthom_construction Pontrjagin-Thom construction
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+construction"} Pontrjagin-Thom construction
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : S^n \to M O
            from an
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            such that if chosen
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transversal+map"} transversal
            to the zero-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi M
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \hookrightarrow M O
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mi n
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi M
                          %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  f^* B &amp;\to&amp; B
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  S^n &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; M O
                  }
          %p
            is a manifold cobordant to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X] \simeq [f^* B]
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
          %p
            By using derived smooth manifolds instead of ordinary smooth manifolds here, the condition that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            be transversal to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            could be dropped.
          %h3#string_topology String topology
          %p (…)
          %h3#floer_homology Floer homology
          %p (…)
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p The following definition characterizes the design criterion for derived smooth manifolds as being objects for which homotopy-intersections
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi X
                  %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mi h
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A \cap_X B := A \times_X^h B
          %p
            preserve the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⌣
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi X
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [A] \smile [B] \simeq [A \cap_X B]
                  \\,.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              We say an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              supports
              %strong derived cup products for cobordisms
              if
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  it is equipped with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi Diff
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        i : Diff \hookrightarrow C
                %p
                  embedding the category of
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %li
                %p
                  for any two submanifolds
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mo ←
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to X \leftarrow B
                  (transversal or not) the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi X
                        %mi B
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        A \cap_X B := i(A) \times_{i(X)} i(B)
                %p
                  exists in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mo ←
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to X \leftarrow B
                  happen to be
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transverse+map"} transverse map
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        i(A \times_X B) \simeq i(A) \times_{i(X)} i(B)
                        \\,,
                %p
                  with the image under
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  of the ordinary
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                  in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
                  on the left;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  preserves the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              %li
                %p (…nice interaction with underlying topological spaces…)
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Diff
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Diff
                  there is a
                  %em derived cobordism ring
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega(X)
                  such that …
              %li
                %p
                  for any submanifolds
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mo ←
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to X \leftarrow B
                  we have
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ⌣
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi X
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [A] \smile [B] = [A \cap_X B]
                %p
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega(X)
                %p (…)
          %p A central statement about derived smooth manifolds will be
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Spivak"}> Spivak, theorem 1.8
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-manifold"} dg-manifold
          %h2#references References
          %p The definition of derived smooth manifolds is indicated at the very end of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Structured+Spaces"} Structured Spaces
              \.
          %p
            A detailed construction and discjussion in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            by
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+T-algebra"} homotopy T-algebra
          %ul
            %li#Spivak08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Spivak"}> David Spivak
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Derived smooth manifolds
              %strong 153
              1 (2010) 22-128 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0810.5174"}> arXiv:0810.5174
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1215/00127094-2010-021"} doi:10.1215/00127094-2010-021
          %p
            Something similar (derived
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Joyce"}> Dominic Joyce
              ,
              %em D-orbifolds, Kuranishi spaces, and polyfolds
              talk notes (Jan 2010) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://people.maths.ox.ac.uk/joyce/dmtalk.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Joyce-DOrbifolds.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Seminar notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Seminar+on+derived+differential+geometry"} Seminar on derived differential geometry
              (2010)
          %p Further developments:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Dennis Borisov, Justin Noel,
                %em Simplicial approach to derived differential manifolds
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1112.0033"}> arXiv:1112.0033
                )
            %li#CarchediSteffens19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Carchedi"}> David Carchedi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pelle+Steffens"} Pelle Steffens
                %em On the universal property of derived manifolds
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.06195"}> arXiv:1905.06195
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
                  of derived smooth manifolds)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Carchedi"}> David Carchedi
                ,
                %em Derived Manifolds as Differential Graded Manifolds
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.11140"}> arXiv:2303.11140
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Taroyan"}> Gregory Taroyan
                ,
                %em Equivalent models of derived stacks
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.12699"}> arXiv:2303.12699
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pelle+Steffens"}> Pelle Steffens
                ,
                %em
                  Derived
                  = succeed "-Geometry" do
